Template: airwatcher/db_password
Type: password
Description: NightWatcher database password:
 AirWatcher stores ASIAir config and copy status in the shared NightWatcher
 (nwdb) database as the 'nightwatcher' user. This password is written to
 /etc/airwatcher/airwatcher.env (mode 0640, read by the service) and is never
 stored in the package or in git.
 .
 Leave blank to set it up yourself later, then re-run: dpkg-reconfigure airwatcher

Template: airwatcher/incoming
Type: string
Default: /astronomy/astro-imaging/incoming
Description: Directory to copy ASIAir frames into:
 Frames pulled off the ASIAirs are written here, where nightwatcher-ingest then
 classifies and files them. The 'airwatcher' service account needs write access
 to it (see the group question below).

Template: airwatcher/web_bind
Type: string
Default: 0.0.0.0
Description: AirWatcher web UI bind address:
 Address for AirWatcher's own web UI + API (a different port from NightWatcher2).
 0.0.0.0 serves the whole network; 127.0.0.1 serves only this machine.

Template: airwatcher/web_port
Type: string
Default: 8686
Description: AirWatcher web UI port:

Template: airwatcher/web_token
Type: password
Description: Web UI access token (optional):
 If set, the web UI/API require this token (entered once in the browser). Leave
 blank for no token. Recommended when binding to 0.0.0.0 on an untrusted network.

Template: airwatcher/discover_subnet
Type: string
Default: 172.22.4.0/24
Description: Default subnet for the ASIAir discovery scan:
 The web UI's "Scan" button and the daemon default to this CIDR when looking for
 ASIAirs (by their control port 4400).

Template: airwatcher/archive_group
Type: string
Description: Group to grant the 'airwatcher' service account (optional):
 The service runs as the unprivileged 'airwatcher' user, which needs write
 access to the incoming directory above. If that directory is group-accessible,
 name the group to add 'airwatcher' to it. Leave blank to arrange access
 yourself (ownership or a filesystem ACL).

Template: airwatcher/start_now
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Start the AirWatcher service now?
 Safe once the database is reachable. You can add ASIAirs afterwards from the web
 UI at http://<host>:<port>/.
